the long wait for wonder woman 1984  is almost over and you can feel the  excitement of the cast and crew  a virtual panel discussion for the much  anticipated sequel kicked off the dc  fandom event with a bang on august 22nd  as gal gadot chris pine kristen wiig  pedro pascal and director patty jenkins  fielded questions from fans across the  globe  including some wonderful surprise guests  jenkins and her cast reminisced fondly  about their time on set together which  must feel almost  as long ago as diana's adventures in  world war 1 after all the delays wonder  woman 1984 has seen  afterward tennis legend and wonder woman  superfan  venus williams joined in to ask a dutt  and wig which of their characters would  win in a tennis match  i think cheetah would win really  while this celebrity game of superhero  what if was nothing short of delightful  and even more special guest was waiting  in the wings  before debuting a brand new trailer for  wonder woman 1984  the fandom panel welcomed the original  on-screen wonder woman herself  the iconic former beauty queen linda  carter  despite the distance between the panel  participants emotions ran high  in the virtual hall of heroes as two  generations of amazons  expressed their appreciation for each  other carter explained that she and wig  have a mutual appreciation  which they intend to seal with a hug as  soon as they can be in the same room  and gushed with praise for jenkins and  godutz take  on diana of themyscira carter became a  tv icon during her three seasons on the  late 70s wonder woman series  and she couldn't be happier that a whole  new generation is looking up to  a whole new diana prince on the big  screen she's seen firsthand what the  character means to fans of the movies  with her own daughter falling under the  spell of good dutt's wonder woman  telling her quote i finally get what  wonder woman means to everyone  she said mom i finally get it  i finally understand why  everyone idolizes you wonder woman 1984  not only takes place in a different era  than the original flick did  but it also shows a new side of the  lasso swinging hero  this time around diana has literal  decades of experience living in the  world of man  and she uses that wisdom to her benefit  in a cover story back in june  good dutt told total film in wonder  woman 1984  she's been around she's wiser she's more  mature  she's guarded she's lost all her friends  throughout the years  but she's still doing the right thing  but she is different than when we last  saw her  in the upcoming sequel diana's beloved  steve trevor played by chris pine  is back after having presumably died a  true hero's death in the first movie  a new face is barbara ann minerva played  by kristen wiig  an archaeologist who works alongside  diana and even forms a friendship with  her  only to turn into diana's foe after a  mishap grants her the powers of a  cheetah  then there's pedro pascal's maxwell lord  a smarmy businessman with a villainous  edge who makes grandiose promises about  granting everyone's wishes  in the new trailer for wonder woman 1984  that also dropped during dc fandom  fans saw lord giving a speech from  within what appeared to be the white  house briefing  room and also spotted him having a  conversation with barbara on air force  one this has led many fans to believe  that lord perhaps  wins a presidential election using his  mysterious  wish-granting artifact to either grant  the public's wishes in exchange for  their votes  or to grant his own wish for more power  the sequel pick features a handful of  actors in yet  undisclosed roles including natasha  rothwell of saturday night live and  insecure fame  grandfather's star ravi patel and mad  men actor christopher pollaha  so there's no telling how many more  allies or antagonists diana will face in  this next adventure  in all it's looking like wonder woman  1984 will be a more than worthy  follow-up flick to the widely adored  original  